    docs(STAS-330): state the run-open consumption seam and the dormant steering-lane guard
    
    Code review F1 (shows vs opens): consumption is recorded when the wake opens the run, not when the prompt renders, so the module header, the heartbeat FNXC block and docs/agents.md now say so and name the graceful-exit boundary (missing card / terminal card / checkout held elsewhere) as accepted, with the executor Steering Comments lane still delivering the row.
    
    Advisories A1/A2: the two reply-detector docstrings no longer claim steering rows carry agent identity (every writer passes the literal user|agent today), and the author-filter test header states that its cast fixtures pin the seam for a future writer-side identity stamp rather than shipped steering behaviour.
    
    Co-authored-by: Fusion <noreply@runfusion.ai>

